From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RockBase <rockbase@k230>
Date: Tue, 15 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: storage: skip TUR for ASMT 2235 on dwc2 host

The ASMT 2235 USB-SATA bridge (0x174c:0x235c) stalls on REQUEST
SENSE transfers when connected to a dwc2 host controller.  Mark
the device as non-removable to skip TEST UNIT READY checks.

Signed-off-by: RockBase <rockbase@k230>
---
 drivers/usb/storage/scsiglue.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/storage/scsiglue.c b/drivers/usb/storage/scsiglue.c
index xxxxxxx..xxxxxxx 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/storage/scsiglue.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/storage/scsiglue.c
@@ -167,6 +167,12 @@
 			break;
 		}
 
+		/* ASMT 2235 on dwc2: REQUEST SENSE transfer stalls, skip TUR */
+		if (us->pusb_dev->descriptor.idVendor == cpu_to_le16(0x174c) &&
+		    us->pusb_dev->descriptor.idProduct == cpu_to_le16(0x235c)) {
+			sdev->removable = 0;
+		}
+
 		/*
 		 * Disk-type devices use MODE SENSE(6) if the protocol
 		 * (SubClass) is Transparent SCSI, otherwise they use
